## SQ-SWL-02 | an old strong Phantom Bane potion reads back as creativebrewing:phantom_bane; removed ids in a chest load with no missing-registry warning
@group A (no old save)
@commands `cdevtest nbt` on a potion with `Potion:"creativeengineering:strong_phantom_bane"`; a chest written with that potion, `rusticdelight:fruit_beignet`, `kubejs:incomplete_quiche_bacon`, `kubejs:incomplete_quiche_mushroom` and a bread; `/data get block`
@pass `potion=creativebrewing:phantom_bane` (not `minecraft:empty`); the chest keeps the potion (its id resolves to Phantom Bane) and the bread, the three removed items are gone; no `Unknown` / missing-registry warning naming any of the five ids. The effect `vinery:jellie` only shows in an old world's registry snapshot (not testable here)
@fails potion=minecraft:empty: the `replaces` entry missing from `better_beacons_potions.json`, or `PotionByNameRemapMixin` not reading it; a warning: the `removed` entry missing from that jar's removed.json
@absent creativeengineering:strong_phantom_bane rusticdelight:fruit_beignet kubejs:incomplete_quiche_bacon kubejs:incomplete_quiche_mushroom vinery:jellie (old or removed ids written on purpose)
@reviewed 2026-11-24
# r1118 (2026-11-18): the SQ-EX-01 pattern (old ids in item NBT on a world of its own)
> forceload add 320 192 335 207
sleep 3
> cdevtest nbt minecraft:potion{Potion:'creativeengineering:strong_phantom_bane'}
expect verb=nbt item=minecraft:potion .*potion=creativebrewing:phantom_bane\b
> setblock 328 -60 200 chest{Items:[{Slot:0b,id:"minecraft:potion",Count:1b,tag:{Potion:"creativeengineering:strong_phantom_bane"}},{Slot:1b,id:"rusticdelight:fruit_beignet",Count:1b},{Slot:2b,id:"kubejs:incomplete_quiche_bacon",Count:1b},{Slot:3b,id:"kubejs:incomplete_quiche_mushroom",Count:1b},{Slot:4b,id:"minecraft:bread",Count:1b}]}
> cdevtest inv 328 -60 200
expect verb=inv slot=\d+ item="?minecraft:potion\*1\{.*phantom_bane
expect verb=inv slot=\d+ item="?minecraft:bread\*1
reject verb=inv slot=\d+ item="?(rusticdelight:fruit_beignet|kubejs:incomplete_quiche_(bacon|mushroom))
shell ! grep -iE "(missing|unknown|unidentified).*(strong_phantom_bane|fruit_beignet|incomplete_quiche_(bacon|mushroom)|vinery:jellie)" logs/latest.log
> setblock 328 -60 200 minecraft:air
reject \[cdevtest\] verb=\S+ done=0
reject (Unknown (block|block type|entity)|Incorrect argument for command|Unknown or incomplete command|That position is not loaded)

